 "name": "Irish national road tolls (M50 and the PPP toll roads)",
 "law": "Roads Act 1993 (Part V) and the toll bye-laws of each scheme, maximum tolls for 2024 as published by Transport Infrastructure Ireland per toll road: goods vehicles over 3,500 kg by axles (2 or 3, 4 or more) on the PPP roads, excluding 23% VAT; on the M50 (no VAT) by weight, at the unregistered price, or the tag price for trucks paying by tag. Heavy goods vehicles use the Dublin Port Tunnel free. Each toll is charged at its plaza (M50: its gantry), placed with OpenStreetMap's toll booths (2026-11-08T21:21:00Z). From TII's pages as the Internet Archive kept them, read in a browser into tools/history/browser/ie-2024.json.",
